Z||000000||GSXPete||08-21-2001||02:26 PM||||Whats up? i am new to this board, and sort of new to fiero's. I've wanted one for a long time, ever since i found one i wanted to buy, but didnt have enough money. instead, i bought a 1990 eclipse GSX (AWD turbo). i loved it. i recently blew the motor a few weeks ago and i am in the process of parting it out. the fiero i wanted long ago is still for sale. its an 87 GT fastback 5 spd. 92k on the clock (most of those miles are going to and from pennsylvania, which is about 1000 miles both ways) the owner made this trip about once a month since he got the car new in 87. since then, he's part of a gowing family, and has driven the car less then a thousand miles in the last year and a half. i've done a little research and just wanted to get a little feedback of how quick these cars are, how easy they are to mod, and how they are for everyday driving? being the owner of a pretty quick car (it took $100 to make it a mid 13 second car), i'm not looking to get that kind of speed, but something respectable. please give me some feedback. thanks alot.<P>btw: sorry for the long post  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||JayUSA77||08-21-2001||02:31 PM||||Welcome to the forum. Get the 87 Gt fastback and have some fun. 13 seconds will take some moding and probably alot more than 100 bucks but it will be worth it in the long run. YOu can put a hole bunch of engines in the fiero including a 3.1, 3.4, 3.8, 3.8SC, and even a V-8 350 SBC. ask around everyone here is prety much willing to help.<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||08-21-2001||02:36 PM||||Pete-<P>First of all, welcome to the forum.  <BR>I've got a modded '87 GT with an Auto (see sig).  As to how easy to mod a Fiero- depends on what you're looking to do.  Use the search function on the top/right corner of the forum page to look for specifics.  People have done things ranging from easy (cold air intakes - K&N, electronic ignition, Bored out TB & Intake plenums, suspension, etc...) through to the complex (engine swaps from 3.1L V6, to 3800 S/C w/Nitrous, to SBC V8, LT1, & Northstar conversions).  It all depends on how much time & money you want (are willing) to invest.  Look around, see what you like, and ask (search first- someone else probably already asked).  If after searching you still don't find what you're looking for- ask. Someone will know!  Enjoy!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||08-21-2001||02:39 PM||||Welcome to the forum.  The Fiero is probably the best platform for modifacations ever. There are so many directions you can take a car that its hard to decide.  Good luck and get the car.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
